ARP Packet Fields

A simplified ARP packet includes:

Field	Example
Hardware Type	Ethernet
Protocol Type	IPv4
Hardware Length	6 bytes
Protocol Length	4 bytes
Operation	Request or Reply
Sender MAC	AA-AA-AA-AA
Sender IP	192.168.1.10
Target MAC	00-00-00-00-00-00 (unknown in a request)
Target IP	192.168.1.20
ARP Cache

You can view the ARP cache on most systems.

Linux
ip neigh

or

arp -a

Example:

192.168.1.1
    lladdr 00:11:22:33:44:55
Windows
arp -a
Why Is ARP Only for Local Networks?

Routers separate networks.

Suppose you want to reach:

8.8.8.8

Your computer does not ARP for Google's MAC address—that device isn't on your local network.

Instead, it ARPs for the default gateway (your router):

192.168.1.1

Then it sends the packet to the router, which forwards it toward the internet.

